  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Caritas Bangladesh gender cell</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to assist the Caritas Bangladesh Gender Cell (CGC) in supporting activities towards gender equality at organisational and at programme level within Caritas. 

CAFOD made an initial grant to CGC in 2011 covering the cost of a Gender Audit, and capacity strengthening activities of the CGC (for which CAFOD provided technical as well as financial support). Subsequently two smaller annual grants were made to support the completion of a three-year workplan 2011-14 under which the recommendations of the Gender Audit were to be implemented and bedded in; Caritas Bangladesh&apos;s policies, codes and guidelines improved; relevant training (e.g. on Gender Sensitivity, Grievance Handling, Women Leadership Development) rolled out to all Caritas staff, and also to others parts of the Catholic Church in Bangladesh and other NGOs; and networking undertaken with relevant actors at local, national and international level to promote gender equality.</narrative>
  </description>
